{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1005519-dark-ages-roads-in-requiem","id":1005519,"title":"Dark Ages Roads in Requiem","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-19T17:22:15-08:00","id":1005519,"title":"Dark Ages Roads in Requiem","content":"Is it possible to port the Dark Ages Roads into Requiem as alternatives to Humanity?<br /> <br /> Or is alternative &quot;morality&quot; even possible?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","name":"Veindark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T18:07:47-08:00","id":1005526,"title":"","content":"I don't see why not. You'd just need a different set of breaking points, and maybe alter your Touchstones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T22:51:23-08:00","id":1005612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1005519-dark-ages-roads-in-requiem?p=1005526#post1005526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see why not. You'd just need a different set of breaking points, and maybe alter your Touchstones.</div> </div> </div> </div>You'd also need to work out how all the various things that key off Humanity would be affected - Banes, Clan weaknesses, sunlight damage, I think a couple of Conditions...<br /> <br /> The thing is, Humanity is actually super central to Requiem. The whole premise of the game is playing out the descent into monstrosity. How human a vampire's worldview and behavior is has a real, measurable effect on them in Requiem, making them, in a very literal sense, less human the lower it falls. So, a Requiem vampire that abandoned Humanity for a Road would pretty much just end up a Draugur.<br /> <br /> If you want to bring Roads into Requiem, I would recommend making them behavior codes that protect Humanity, kind of like Touchstones, rather than Humanity replacements. In fact, they would probably work just fine as actual Touchstones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T23:07:08-08:00","id":1005619,"title":"","content":"Alternatively if you were interested in putting more work into it you could have different things a vampire could become other than draugr. Similar to how there was the alternate 'Other' instead of the 'Beast' one book had an option for.<br /> <br /> It really detracts from the game as a whole and gets rid of a lot of the themes and moods, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T23:08:49-08:00","id":1005621,"title":"","content":"To be honest I don't really care much about the themes and moods of the game, I just want to play as a vampire and that's it.<br /> <br /> Anyways I think there's examples of Vampire medium that don't have humanity/path/road systems or the whole &quot;personal horror&quot; theme like the WoD does which to be honest, I find humanity (including paths and roads) to be confining and restricting and not really realistic in practice. It's not like the personal horror theme is a requirement for Vampire fiction anyways since I think there's ways to do without it.<br /> <br /> Which Requiem's case, it seems you can't even use your disciplines or even be a vampire which makes it far easier falling into Draugrhood (as if it's pretty inevitable making the game pointless to play) than becoming a Wight in Masquerade.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12524,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","user":"Veindark","date":". 11-20-2016, 02:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","name":"Veindark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T23:13:25-08:00","id":1005623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Veindark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1005519-dark-ages-roads-in-requiem?p=1005621#post1005621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just want to play as a vampire and that's it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not quite true, you want to play a specific sort of vampire.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Anyways I think there's examples of Vampire fiction that don't have humanity/path/road systems like the WoD does. </div> </div> </div>There are indeed, though in much of the fiction you can see vampires dealing with their humanity one way or another.<br /> <br /> The question would be better served by asking your storyteller. It's a modular system and you can do pretty much anything with it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Which Reqiuem's case, it seems you can't even use your discplines or even be a vampire which makes it far easier falling into Draugrhood than becoming a Wight in Masquerade. </div> </div> </div>Does your book say 'Using a Discipline' is a Humanity 1 Breaking Point?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-20-2016, 02:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T23:24:26-08:00","id":1005625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1005519-dark-ages-roads-in-requiem?p=1005623#post1005623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does your book say 'Using a Discipline' is a Humanity 1 Breaking Point?</div> </div> </div> </div>I never said that, I just said that using disciplines is one of the humanity breaking points and plus I would like to make note that even surviving for 500 years is a humanity 2 breaking point which means even being a vampire is a breaking point since it looks like dropping into draugrhood looks pretty inevitable sooner or later even if it takes a thousand years but it's gonna happen anyways making the game pointless to play in the end since it kinda defeats the entire purpose of Vampires being immortal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12524,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","user":"Veindark","date":". 11-20-2016, 02:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","name":"Veindark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T09:02:17-08:00","id":1005724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Veindark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1005519-dark-ages-roads-in-requiem?p=1005621#post1005621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be honest I don't really care much about the themes and moods of the game, I just want to play as a vampire and that's it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Umm ok? Requiem does allow you to play as a vampire, so it seems like your issue is less one of not caring about Requiem's theme and mood, and more of actively disliking them. Now, there's nothing wrong with wanting to play as a vampire with <i>different</i> theme and mood, but Requiem is designed with particular themes and mood in mind, and it's mechanics lend themselves to that, so if you want to change them, you're also going to have to hack the game about. Which again, is fine if that's what you want to do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Veindark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1005519-dark-ages-roads-in-requiem?p=1005621#post1005621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyways I think there's examples of Vampire medium that don't have humanity/path/road systems or the whole &amp;quot;personal horror&amp;quot; theme like the WoD does</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course there are. Requiem is not meant to emulate those examples. Not that you can't use it to emulate them if you want to, but you are going to have to do a little work to accomplish that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Veindark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1005519-dark-ages-roads-in-requiem?p=1005621#post1005621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">which to be honest, I find humanity (including paths and roads) to be confining and restricting and not really realistic in practice.</div> </div> </div> </div>So don't use Humanity. You'll have to decide what to do about the mechanics that key off of Humanity, like Banes, Clan weaknesses, sunlight damage, some of the Conditions, etc. but there's no reason you can't make those changes if that's what you want to do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Veindark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1005519-dark-ages-roads-in-requiem?p=1005621#post1005621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not like the personal horror theme is a requirement for Vampire fiction anyways since I think there's ways to do without it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, but it is a default assumption of Requiem. You don't have to play it that way if you don't want to, but you will be fighting the game's design at times, case in point being Humanity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Veindark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1005519-dark-ages-roads-in-requiem?p=1005621#post1005621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which Requiem's case, it seems you can't even use your disciplines or even be a vampire which makes it far easier falling into Draugrhood (as if it's pretty inevitable making the game pointless to play) than becoming a Wight in Masquerade.</div> </div> </div> </div>Humanity Breaking Points are tiered for a reason. The lower your Humanity falls, the fewer things count as Breaking Points. The more monstrous you become, the easier it is to act like a monster without becoming less human than you already are.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Veindark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1005519-dark-ages-roads-in-requiem?p=1005625#post1005625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never said that, I just said that using disciplines is one of the humanity breaking points</div> </div> </div> </div>All of the Breaking Points that explicitly refer to Discipline use are above Humanity 7, which is default starting Humanity, so they won't even have any effect on play unless you've got a player who actually buys their Humanity up above starting with Experiences.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Veindark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1005519-dark-ages-roads-in-requiem?p=1005625#post1005625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and plus I would like to make note that even surviving for 500 years is a humanity 2 breaking point which means even being a vampire is a breaking point since it looks like dropping into draugrhood looks pretty inevitable sooner or later even if it takes a thousand years but it's gonna happen anyways making the game pointless to play in the end since it kinda defeats the entire purpose of Vampires being immortal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, first of all, it's a Breaking Point at Humanity 2. Meaning if your Humanity is 1 it's not a Breaking Point for you. Meaning it is literally impossible to become a Draugur from old age alone, you have to at least go a decade without human contact, kill your own Touchstone, commit heinous, spree, or mass murder, Diablerize another vampire, or Embrace a human. And in all but the last case, you also have to fail the roll, which you'll have at least one die for if you still have an attatched Touchstone. If you're really that worried, you could always just take a Bane for each of the three Humanity 1 Breaking Points and never commit Diablerie or Embrace. And anyway, who just sits at Humanity 1? You can raise your Humanity for a measly two Experiences, so it's not inevitable at all. You can prolong it indefinitely if you so choose.<br /> <br /> I also think it's a little ironic complaining that being a vampire makes you lose Humanity, considering that's precisely the intent. Vampires aren't human. Being one <i>should</i> make you less human, by definition. But, whatever, you don't like the mechanic, and you don't need any more reason than that to remove it from your game. By all means, excise Humanity, or modify it, or replace it with Roads, or leave it be and get rid of Draugur as the end-state, what ever you want to do. No one is stopping you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T08:19:34-08:00","id":1006201,"title":"","content":"Charlaquin has provided [her] usual excellent advice. The main answer to your original question is &quot;yes, it's possible&quot;--you can rip out humanity and flat-out replace it with a path if you want and your storyteller agrees. There are some things you'll want to be aware of:<br /> <br /> 1. Please keep in mind that in VtM roads/paths were expressly monstrous in nature. Vampires taking them as their way of handling the mental+moral strain of unlife had to run down their humanity and then carefully adopt the new Path and build it up. The reward was freeing themselves of the shackles of <u>moral</u> concerns VtM was tied to, however the consequences of a Path remained that <u>the vampire had an effective Humanity of 1</u> as far as system interactions went--she was a monster, just wasn't in danger of losing her mind.<br /> <br /> 2. VtR 2e assumes that you're playing against the trope of &quot;I don't want to become a complete monster because then I lose my mind&quot;. If your character can cut a deal with his beast such that it's happy with you behaving in a different way, and you're happy not being human, then cool.<br /> <br /> There's several ways you could accomplish this. The easiest is just to scribble out &quot;Humanity&quot; print off a list of your path's replacement sins, and assume you have Humanity 1 for everything except Degeneration rolls. This will bork you for Theben Sorcery, but Road of Heaven could flip the logic and treat your Path level as Humanity (treating it as 10 for Cruic?). You can do this, handwave the rest on the fly, and probably have a fulfilling vampire experience reveling in the night so long as everyone at the table agrees.<br /> <br /> Another way others have suggested is to treat your Path/Road as a merit that acts as a Touchstone. Now Touchstones are meant to represent things your vampire spends attention on, and have a risk associated with--they stabilize the character and remind her of her purpose and what it means to be her. The default assumption is that &quot;to be her&quot; refers to humanity and human connection, but not necessarily (or, not so directly). You could run the Path Merit from 1-5, adding a Touchstone at each rank along with two of the Path's &quot;sins&quot; in ascending order. Road of Kings would then include at Merit rank 1: <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table_wiki-content-table\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_wiki-content-table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_wiki-content-table_td\">2</td> <td class=\"text_table_wiki-content-table_td\">Breaking your word to your superiors</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_wiki-content-table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_wiki-content-table_td\">1</td> <td class=\"text_table_wiki-content-table_td\">Breaking a sworn oath</td> </tr> </table></div> Merit rank 2 would add sins for Road level 3 and 4, and etc. Violating any of these sins would force a roll of the Merit level, to avoid detaching the highest attached Path-merit touchstone. Subtract the path level from your Humanity score to determine social penalties for interacting with mortals.<br /> <br /> A third approach is similar to the second, only instead of adding touchstones, the Path-merit removes a breaking point per level as if it were a bane taken, substituting the Path's sins for the bane. Breaking points removed cannot be actions otherwise forbidden by the Path.<br /> <br /> Personally? I'm still not sure any of this is really needed; it adds complexity and muddles some of the charming clarity of VtR vampiric existence, in which Humanity is not that expensive to build up and you can take Touchstones for virtually whatever you could think of. --I could build a 7,000-year old NPC (let's call her &quot;Morrigu&quot;) from Doggerland whose touchstone is &quot;Celtic standing stones&quot; (or, a particular one) representing vestiges of ancient worship practices, and it'd work fine. She'd hover around 2-4 Humanity for millennia.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12493,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","user":"Khanwulf","date":". 11-21-2016, 11:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T09:53:23-08:00","id":1006246,"title":"","content":"I would personally recommend Requiem 1st edition, humanity there was less intrusive mechanically and could be easily removed.<br /> <br /> As for the Dark ages roads there is not as clean cut, each path should be taken as their own thing and though what would and wouldnt constitute a breaking point.<br /> <br /> But if you wanna just play vampire and not having to worry about enforcing humanity mechanically the easiest way is with the mechanics attached is <br /> <br /> Clan weakness is always present, pick one set damage for sunlight (i dont remember which was the standard in 1s) and as for banes you could make them into flaws PCs can take at chargen.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T10:56:33-08:00","id":1006283,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12493_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12493\" data-vbnamecard=\"12493\">Khanwulf</a>: just curious, why the brackets around [her]?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T07:06:48-08:00","id":1006691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1005519-dark-ages-roads-in-requiem?p=1006283#post1006283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12493_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12493\" data-vbnamecard=\"12493\">Khanwulf</a>: just curious, why the brackets around [her]?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I've never seen a specific, self-reference to your gender, and assuming from the forum icon wanted to demonstrate that assumption. <br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T07:43:18-08:00","id":1006704,"title":"","content":"I usually try to just call everyone &quot;they&quot;. Man, woman, four squirrels in a trench coat, it matters not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T10:58:57-08:00","id":1006771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1005519-dark-ages-roads-in-requiem?p=1006691#post1006691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've never seen a specific, self-reference to your gender, and assuming from the forum icon wanted to demonstrate that assumption. <br /> <br /> --Khanwulf</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, that was what I figured, but just wanted to make sure. Your assumption was correct, she/her/hers <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-24T13:34:40-08:00","id":1007825,"title":"","content":"I don't think it's impossible, though it takes away most of the themes of Vampire: The Requiem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T16:27:49-08:00","id":1011726,"title":"","content":"One thing I like here is to actually wright in a language with neutral gender. It isn't possible in portuguese.<br /> <br /> The advice of Charlaquin is really useful, though I don't find it so much of a problem. I personally like Humanity, always liked, but the game won't be too damaged by not using it.<br /> <br /> What I want to add is:<br /> <br /> First, DA Roads aren't monstrous as a whole, only a couple of them actually are that much of a problem. That's their main distinction from modern Paths in Masquerade.<br /> <br /> Second, aside the aforementioned use of Roads instead of Humanity or as Touchstones, you can use them as Banes, or complement with Banes.<br /> <br /> And to get completely rid of Humanity, the easiest way is to simply default all the derived stuff to whatever level you want, if you're the ST. If you have any doubt, use &quot;as if Humanity 7&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T22:34:06-08:00","id":1011865,"title":"","content":"Thus thread got me wondering... From my reading of Humanity in VtR 2e, it seems it functions as a measure of how distanced you are from your mortal self.<br /> <br /> The Breaking Points provided are examples you are meant to customize. So, a mortal assassin could have a Breaking Point of, say, declining a job offer for the same of Kindred responsibilities (or even, fail to kill for a long time).<br /> <br /> I mean, wasn't that the purpose of all neonates starting at 7? I might be wrong here...<br /> <br /> So my suggestion would be to turn Roads on their heads. People brought up as members of the aristocracy would have something that resembled the Road of Kings, albeit customized to accommodate the character's mortal experiences and essence...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.greece-bynight.com\" target=\"_blank\">Greece By Night LARP</a>","edited":{"userid":59,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","user":"stylanski","date":". 12-04-2016, 01:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","name":"stylanski","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar59_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"299"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T16:26:13-08:00","id":1012242,"title":"","content":"I agree, though it should be done with caution. Humanity is described as two things, mostly: your distance from your former self and your ability to mimic mortality. But the mechanics aren't always good at delivering it, and the greater problem that I see is the seemingly fixed set of Breaking Points. I think that the idea of using Roads as a basis is sound, at least until better rules for customizing the BP set appear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}